  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Given that  $({s}^{2}+2s-1)({s}^{2}-s+2)={s}^{4}+a{s}^{3}+b{s}^{2}+cs-2,$ calculate $a+b+c.$",
  "worked_solution": "We distribute all three terms of the trinomial in the first set of parentheses to the trinomial in the second set of parentheses. Then, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({s}^{2}+2s-1)({s}^{2}-s+2) & = \\\\ {s}^{2}({s}^{2}-s+2)+2s({s}^{2}-s+2)-1({s}^{2}-s+2) & = \\\\ {s}^{4}-{s}^{3}+2{s}^{2}+2{s}^{3}-2{s}^{2}+4s-{s}^{2}+s-2 & = \\\\ {s}^{4}+{s}^{3}-{s}^{2}+5s-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ $b=-1,$ and $c=5.$ So, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+(-1)+5=5.\n$$",
